STEP 05: Create the KEDA ScaledObject

- For this first exercise, we'll configure KEDA to monitor CPU utilization and scale demo-app between one and three replicas.
- One important detail: CPU-based scaling is normally handled by Kubernetes HPA. We're using it here to learn how KEDA creates and manages an HPA. Later,
we'll do a queue-based example to understand KEDA's real advantage.


scaledobject.yaml

apiVersion: keda.sh/v1alpha1
kind: ScaledObject
metadata:
  name: demo-app-scaler
  namespace: keda-lab
spec:
  scaleTargetRef:
    name: demo-app

  minReplicaCount: 1
  maxReplicaCount: 3

  triggers:
    - type: cpu
      metricType: Utilization
      metadata:
        value: "50"


# kubectl apply -f scaledobject.yaml                                                                                                                  
scaledobject.keda.sh/demo-app-scaler created


# kubectl get ScaledObject -n keda-lab
