STEP 06: Let's generate CPU load

- NGINX serving ordinary requests may not consume enough CPU to trigger scaling. We'll deliberately generate CPU work inside the pod.

1. Generate CPU load inside demo-app
    - Run this command to start a CPU-consuming process inside your existing NGINX pod:
    # kubectl exec -n keda-lab demo-app-74498c7cd4-xf7fh -- sh -c 'for i in 1 2 3 4; do (while true; do :; done) & done; sleep 300'
    - This starts four CPU-consuming loops inside the container for five minutes.


